This guide covers the quickest way to install Java (JDK 21 or 23) on Windows and macOS.
1. Download the JDKOfficial Source: Visit the Oracle Java Downloads page.
  Select Version: Choose the latest LTS (Long Term Support) version (e.g., JDK 21) or the newest version (e.g., JDK 23).
  Download: Select your operating system (Windows/macOS) and download the x64 Installer (.exe for Windows, .dmg for Mac).
2. InstallWindows: Run the .exe file. Click "Next" through the installer.
  Take note of the installation path (usually C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-...).
  macOS: Open the .dmg file, double-click the .pkg file, and follow the instructions.
3. Set Environment Variables (Windows)Search for "Environment Variables" in the Windows search bar and select "Edit the system environment variables".
Click Environment Variables.Under System Variables, click New, set Name to JAVA_HOME and Value to the path of your JDK installation (e.g., C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-23).
Find the Path variable, select it, click Edit, then New and add: %JAVA_HOME%\bin.Click OK on all windows to save.4. Verify InstallationOpen your terminal (Command Prompt on Windows, Terminal on Mac) and run the following command:
    bashjava -version
If successful, you will see the Java version details (e.g., java version "23...").
